A||||8||86SE||Guess what I got Beat by last night!!||||13||
Z||000000||86SE||09-02-2000||02:38 PM||||Well, 2 nights ago I hammered a V6 stang, and low and behold last night I saw a 5 spoke Mustang roll into town.  A Mustang GT! It was a red/maroon '96 4.6L V8 auto stang.  I asked him if he wanted to race, and he thought <B>I</B>was going to beat him because I had the smaller car!  <P>Anyway, I finally talked him into racing. So we drove out to the race spot, I took the left lane, he took the right.  The first run wasent very close, he got a good jump on me and pulled a car legnth on me before I got to second.  We went about 100 and he was about 4-4.5 car legnths ahead of me.  So we turned around and he wanted a fair race back to town.  We pulled up nose to nose, I put her to the wood in first gear, I held the Mustang at my door until 80!!  At about 75 the stang pulled a car legnth on me, and thats it!<P>There was about 15 witnesses in various cars behind us that tried to keep up, they were all 1/4 mile behind us.<P>On guy was in a newer 3.4L buick and he said he was right behind me and he florred it when I did and I pulled away from him like a bat outta hell.<P>Anyways, Im happy, I finally got to race a V8 Mustang and gave him a run for his money.  Finally got a CHALLENGE around here, v6 stangs just suck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And don't talk about weight differences, a V8 Mustang is a V8 Mustang and a Fiero beat it to 60.  Could be the driver, but I highly doubt it, I could hear his engine roaring over mine and it was running really high in the RPM's.<P>Next month I told him to find me with my 3.4 and then we will race, I have the feeling I will beat him....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention<p>[This message has been edited by 86SE (edited 09-02-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||09-02-2000||04:25 PM||||FWIW, the 96-98 V8 (4.6L) stangs were the slowest (espically with automatic) stangs from 1985 to present.  Its unusual you found one apparently bone stock.<P>I won't talk about weight or even street racing, but if you really want a 'challenge', then I'd suggest going to your local dragstrip and picking on some of those Stangs, I'm sure they would be interested.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||09-03-2000||02:58 AM||||I guarentee any 5 speed v-6 Fiero, even a 4 speed could have easily beat the Mustang.  I know I dont stand a chance against drag stangs, do you think im crazy, stock Fiero vs modifyed mustangs?<P>The 4.6 was a challenge enough for me, hes got 80% more power then me and a TON more torque.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
